and regulations. Applicants must be lawfully authorized to work for any employer in the United States. We are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa for this position Position Summary Implement, maintain, and support security and transaction system hardware and software. Provide technical support to security and transaction system end users, troubleshoot system-related issues, and contribute to the continual enhancement and improvement of security and transaction systems. Principal Duties & Responsibilities Administer access control and mobile access system hardware and software. Administer surveillance system hardware and software. Administer transaction system hardware and software. Upgrade and institute policies and procedures to improve the level of service provided to the security and transaction system users. Train the community on equipment usage. Answer support questions from end users and research problems. Monitor and manage how the level 1 helpdesk responds to issues as it pertains to the equipment and services that we support and maintain; produce monthly status reports. Troubleshoot hardware and software problems. Monitor network resources, assuring continuous availability and service. Maintain department websites, ensuring that they are up to date and easy to navigate. Other duties as assigned Knowledge, Skills, Abilities & Other Attributes Bachelor's degree required; degree in a technical field preferred. Two years' experience in an information technology position. Knowledge of access control equipment and how it operates Knowledge of surveillance equipment and how it operates Proficiency with operating systems and software found on campus: Windows Server and Workstation, MS Office Good interpersonal skills in dealing with a diverse community Ability to assume project leadership Evidence of experience in performing duties and responsibilities with minimal supervision; along with the ability to communicate verbally and in writing Must be able to track and stay updated on multiple tasks at the same time Experience with computer hardware and software installations and troubleshooting is required Unusual Working Conditions Working after hours and over the weekend to provide support and complete assigned tasks are sometimes required Pre-Employment Requirements All offers of employment are contingent upon satisfactory completion of a background check. Compensation & Benefits : The salary range for this position is $56,930 - $66,040 Sacred Heart University offers eligible employees a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, vision, life insurance, disability, retirement, paid time off, and other employee benefits. Specific benefits and eligibility requirements may vary based on the position and applicable plan provisions. This job posting provides an overview of the role's general nature and expected tasks. It is not meant to be a comprehensive list of all duties performed. The university reserves the right to modify or reassign job responsibilities at any time. This posting description does not constitute an employment contract, either explicit or implied. Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Staff Job Function Information Technology Pay Type Salary Education Level Bachelor\u2019s Degree Scan this QR code and apply! Download 3135 Easton Turnpike, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA \u00a92009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Cookie Preferences Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"}, "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/shu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/8027": {"title": "Information Technology", "description": "Information Technology - Systems Analyst, Finance | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs English (United States) Sign In Information Technology - Systems Analyst, Finance Req #918 5151 Park Ave, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA Apply Share Job Description Posted Thursday, October 1, 2026 at 9:00 PM About Sacred Heart University As one of the nation\u2019s largest Catholic universities and among the fastest-growing private doctoral institutions in the U.S., Sacred Heart University is a national leader in shaping higher education for the 21st century. SHU offers more than 100 undergraduate, graduate and doctoral programs on its Fairfield, Conn., campus. Sacred Heart also has a campus in Dingle, Ireland, and offers online programs. Nearly 10,000 students attend the University\u2019s nine colleges and schools: College of Arts & Sciences; School of Communication, Media & the Arts; School of Social Work; School of Computing & Engineering; School of Performing Arts; College of Health Professions; the Isabelle Farrington College of Education & Human Development; the Jack Welch College of Business & Technology; and the Dr. Susan L. Davis, RN, & Richard J. Henley College of Nursing. Sacred Heart, a Laudato Si\u2019 campus, stands out from other Catholic universities as it was established to be led by the laity. This contemporary Catholic university is rooted in the rich Catholic intellectual tradition and the liberal arts and, at the same time, cultivates students to be forward thinkers who enact change in their own lives, professions, and communities.\u202fSacred Heart University has earned national recognition for academic excellence, student success, career outcomes, and campus experience. The Princeton Review recognized SHU in its Best 392 Colleges: 2027 Edition and Best Business Schools: 2027 Edition, while additional national recognitions highlight the University\u2019s commitment to preparing students for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Sacred Heart is home to the award-winning, NPR-affiliate station, WSHU Public Radio; Division I athletics; and an impressive performing arts program that includes choir, band, dance, and theatre . www.sacredheart.edu View SHU\u2019s Faculty Experts Here To apply: Qualified candidates are invited to submit a completed application and r\u00e9sum\u00e9 through the University's online application system. Applications submitted outside of the official Careers at SHU website will not be considered. Applicants should not apply through third-party or external job sites, as such postings may be fraudulent or may misrepresent opportunities that are no longer available at the University. A cover letter or statement of interest is preferred for all staff positions. Sacred Heart University complies with all federal and state employment laws and regulations. Applicants must be lawfully authorized to work for any employer in the United States. We are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa for this position Position Summary Provide system administration, support, and systems analysis of assigned applications. Provide level 2 software application support for the university user community. Resource for level 1 system analyst to ensure timely resolution of tickets.\u00a0This is a 100% on-campus position. Principal Duties & Responsibilities Monitor, maintain, and coordinate minor upgrades for technology systems in assigned responsibility areas, including problem-solving and implementing system modifications. Coordinate the execution of user acceptance testing procedures and develop test cases to serve the overall quality assurance process. Analyze business process issues and/or problems and provide consulting assistance to system users; conduct research on possible solutions and make recommendations based on findings; suggest, design, test, implement, and evaluate solutions. Brainstorm new ways to add more functionality to systems Coordinate creation, updates, and retirement of interfaces for supported applications Demonstrate thorough and friendly customer service to the university community Communicate clearly and professionally, both verbally and in writing, to different audiences May perform all or some of the responsibilities above and other related duties as assigned Knowledge, Skills, Abilities & Other Attributes Bachelor\u2019s Degree in a computer-related or business-related discipline required Minimum 2 years experience in system administration, level 2 application support, and troubleshooting Experience with and understanding of academic environment and familiarity with academic-related applications preferred Excellent analytical and problem-solving skills Exceptional verbal and written communication skills, as well as strong interpersonal skills Excellent organizational skills and attention to detail Possess a strong work ethic and team player mentality Ability to take initiative and be self-motivated, as well as collaborate successfully with a team Familiarity with Ellucian Colleague Systems Experience with Financial Applications Ability to work on campus full-time Unusual Working Conditions Working after hours, on weekends, and holidays to complete assigned tasks is sometimes required. Pre-Employment Requirements All offers of employment are contingent upon satisfactory completion of a background check. Compensation & Benefits : The salary range for this position is $65,460 - 72,420 Sacred Heart University offers eligible employees a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, vision, life insurance, disability, retirement, paid time off, and other employee benefits. Specific benefits and eligibility requirements may vary based on the