., Sacred Heart University is a national leader in shaping higher education for the 21st century. SHU offers more than 100 undergraduate, graduate and doctoral programs on its Fairfield, Conn., campus. Sacred Heart also has a campus in Dingle, Ireland, and offers online programs. Nearly 10,000 students attend the University\u2019s nine colleges and schools: College of Arts & Sciences; School of Communication, Media & the Arts; School of Social Work; School of Computing & Engineering; School of Performing Arts; College of Health Professions; the Isabelle Farrington College of Education & Human Development; the Jack Welch College of Business & Technology; and the Dr. Susan L. Davis, RN, & Richard J. Henley College of Nursing. Sacred Heart, a Laudato Si\u2019 campus, stands out from other Catholic universities as it was established to be led by the laity. This contemporary Catholic university is rooted in the rich Catholic intellectual tradition and the liberal arts and, at the same time, cultivates students to be forward thinkers who enact change in their own lives, professions, and communities.\u202fSacred Heart University has earned national recognition for academic excellence, student success, career outcomes, and campus experience. The Princeton Review recognized SHU in its Best 392 Colleges: 2027 Edition and Best Business Schools: 2027 Edition, while additional national recognitions highlight the University\u2019s commitment to preparing students for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Sacred Heart is home to the award-winning, NPR-affiliate station, WSHU Public Radio; Division I athletics; and an impressive performing arts program that includes choir, band, dance, and theatre . www.sacredheart.edu View SHU\u2019s Faculty Experts Here To apply: Qualified candidates are invited to submit a completed application and r\u00e9sum\u00e9 through the University's online application system. Applications submitted outside of the official Careers at SHU website will not be considered. Applicants should not apply through third-party or external job sites, as such postings may be fraudulent or may misrepresent opportunities that are no longer available at the University. A cover letter or statement of interest is preferred for all staff positions. Sacred Heart University complies with all federal and state employment laws and regulations. Applicants must be lawfully authorized to work for any employer in the United States. We are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa for this position Position Summary Assist in covering all of Sacred Heart's varsity sports and serve as the primary contact for selected sports, including men\u2019s basketball. The assistant director will serve as the liaison among the media, student-athletes, and coaches. Principal Duties & Responsibilities Serve as the primary athletic communications for assigned athletic programs including men\u2019s basketball. Coordinate all aspects of publicity efforts for assigned sports, including but not limited to - in-game and historical statistics, preparation and dissemination of information to the media and promotion of student-athletes and coaches to media and for postseason and weekly awards. Work closely with production staff on ESPN+ and other broadcasts, assist in production of content for YouTube, social media and in-game video board content. Maintain the athletic website with pre- and post-game stories, stats, records, etc. Assist in maintaining areas of the website not directly associated with teams, i.e. Staff Directory, Compliance Pages, Academic Pages, etc. Assist in the hiring and management of work study student assistants and interns. Participate in creation and implementation of department social media strategy and campaigns to increase publicity and event attendance. Serve as key strategist and producer for the creation of engaging content to promote events, accolades, awards and recognition of Sacred Heart Athletics. Provide support as member of stat crews, public address announcer, etc. Help maintain historical records and archives to produce content on alumni and past teams. Serve as a key member of Athletics Department Communications and Marketing team that makes decisions shaping the department\u2019s communication. Assist in providing creative direction within the Communications and Marketing team, facilitating a cohesive execution of creative materials, including in the creation of the Annual Report. Supervise Communications Game Day Staff. Other duties as assigned Knowledge, Skills, Abilities & Other Attributes Bachelor\u2019s degree and/or equivalent, in communications, journalism, sports management or a related field of study. 4-5 years of experience in a college or professional athletic setting as graduate assistant, full-time intern or full-time. Candidates should have strong oral and writing skills, proficiency in desktop publishing (Adobe InDesign, Photoshop, etc.), experience with in-game statistical software (Genius & StatCrew) new media applications (Instagram Twitter, etc.) and basic computer applications. Advanced proficiency in writing and interviewing with knowledge of the Adobe Creative Suite, specifically Premiere Pro and Photoshop. Advanced proficiency in use and knowledge of all social media platforms, specifically Facebook, Instagram, and Twitter. Proficient knowledge of graphics, photography, video editing. Must possess a valid state-issued driver\u2019s license with a clean driving record. Unusual Working Conditions Full-time position. Nights, weekends, and some travel required. Pre-Employment Requirements All offers of employment are contingent upon satisfactory completion of a background check. Compensation & Benefits : The salary range for this position is $47,050 - $58,960 Sacred Heart University offers eligible employees a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, vision, life insurance, disability, retirement, paid time off, and other employee benefits. Specific benefits and eligibility requirements may vary based on the position and applicable plan provisions. This job posting provides an overview of the role's general nature and expected tasks. It is not meant to be a comprehensive list of all duties performed. The university reserves the right to modify or reassign job responsibilities at any time. This posting description does not constitute an employment contract, either explicit or implied. Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Staff Pay Type Salary Education Level Bachelor\u2019s Degree Scan this QR code and apply! Download 5151 Park Ave, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA \u00a92009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Cookie Preferences Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"}, "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/shu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/8006": {"title": "Business Office", "description": "Business Office - Accountant II | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs English (United States) Sign In Business Office - Accountant II Req #920 3135 Easton Turnpike, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA Apply Share Job Description Posted Thursday, October 1, 2026 at 9:00 PM About Sacred Heart University As one of the nation\u2019s largest Catholic universities and among the fastest-growing private doctoral institutions in the U.S., Sacred Heart University is a national leader in shaping higher education for the 21st century. SHU offers more than 100 undergraduate, graduate and doctoral programs on its Fairfield, Conn., campus. Sacred Heart also has a campus in Dingle, Ireland, and offers online programs. Nearly 10,000 students attend the University\u2019s nine colleges and schools: College of Arts & Sciences; School of Communication, Media & the Arts; School of Social Work; School of Computing & Engineering; School of Performing Arts; College of Health Professions; the Isabelle Farrington College of Education & Human Development; the Jack Welch College of Business & Technology; and the Dr. Susan L. Davis, RN, & Richard J. Henley College of Nursing. Sacred Heart, a Laudato Si\u2019 campus, stands out from other Catholic universities as it was established to be led by the laity. This contemporary Catholic university is rooted in the rich Catholic intellectual tradition and the liberal arts and, at the same time, cultivates students to be forward thinkers who enact change in their own lives, professions, and communities.\u202fSacred Heart University has earned national recognition for academic excellence, student success, career outcomes, and campus experience. The Princeton Review recognized SHU in its Best 392 Colleges: 2027 Edition and Best Business Schools: 2027 Edition, while additional national recognitions highlight the University\u2019s commitment to preparing students for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Sacred Heart is home to the award-winning, NPR-affiliate station, WSHU Public Radio; Division I athletics; and an impressive performing arts program that includes choir, band, dance, and theatre . www.sacredheart.edu View SHU\u2019s Faculty Experts Here To apply: Qualified candidates are invited to submit a completed application and r\u00e9sum\u00e9 through the University's online application system. Applications submitted outside of the official Careers at SHU website will not be considered. Applicants should not apply through third-party or external job sites, as such postings may be fraudulent or may misrepresent opportunities that are no longer available at the University. A cover letter or statement of interest is preferred for all staff positions. Sacred Heart University complies with all federal and state employment laws and regulations. Applicants must be lawfully authorized to work for any employer in the United States. We are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa for this position Position Summary The Accountant II supports accounting operations across multiple functional areas by assisting with the accurate recording, reconciliation, analysis, and reporting of financial activity. This role helps ensure the integrity of the general ledger and supports timely and accurate financial reporting in accordance with established policies and procedures. The position requires solid analytical skills to review account activity, evaluate trends and variances, support estimates and accruals, and identify issues requiring further research or resolution. Additionally, the Accountant II assists in monitoring and reporting the University\u2019s actual results, preparing ad hoc financial analysis, and responding to internal and external financial requests. Principal Duties & Responsibilities Account Reconciliations and Analysis: Own assigned balance sheet and general ledger account reconciliations, including cash and cash equivalents, accrued liabilities, allowance for doubtful accounts, and other assigned accounts. Analyze account activity, research reconciling items, identify trends or unusual transactions, and coordinate with internal departments to resolve discrepancies timely and accurately. Journal Entries and Month-End Close Support: Prepare, review, and post routine and recurring journal entries, including accruals, reversals, expense allocations, revenue activity, and other supporting adjustments. Ensure entries are properly supported, accurately classified, and recorded in accordance with accounting policies and month-end close timelines. Variance Analysis and Financial Review: Perform account-level variance analysis to support the accuracy and completeness of financial records. Review fluctuations against expectations, investigate discrepancies, summarize findings, and escalate items requiring further research or corrective action. General Ledger Maintenance and Governance: Support general ledger governance through account setup, chart of accounts maintenance, account review, and validation of appropriate account usage. Assist in maintaining consistent accounting structure and supporting documentation across departments and financial processes. Compliance and Internal Controls: Follow and reinforce established accounting procedures and internal controls to support accurate, complete, and compliant financial reporting. Assist with approval reviews, compliance checks, documentation requests, and process improvements that strengthen accountability and reduce financial risk. Audit and External Reporting Support: Support the annual audit process by preparing schedules, gathering supporting documentation, responding to audit inquiries, and researching assigned items. Assist with external reporting requests and other compliance-related reviews as needed. NCAA and Agreed-Upon Procedures Support: Assist with the annual NCAA agreed-upon procedures process by compiling supporting documentation, reviewing assigned financial activity, responding to requests, and coordinating follow-up items to ensure timely completion Customer Service and Cross-Functional Support: Monitor and respond to inbound requests from University departments related to journal entries, account reconciliations, general ledger activity, and other accounting matters. Partner with internal stakeholders to research issues, provide guidance, and ensure timely and accurate resolution in accordance with Business Office procedures. Additional Responsibilities : Perform other accounting, analysis, reporting, and special project duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities, & Other Characteristics Bachelor\u2019s degree in Accounting CPA or MBA desired, not required Minimum 2-3 years of related experience. Advanced working knowledge of Excel. Excellent analytical, interpersonal, communication, problem-solving, and organizational skills. Knowledge of accounting software programming desired. Ability to learn new responsibilities, to work independently and as part of a team. Pre-Employment Requirements All offers of employment are contingent upon satisfactory completion of a background check. Compensation & Benefits : The salary range for this position is $56,930 - $80,000 Sacred Heart University offers eligible employees a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, vision, life insurance, disability, retirement, paid time off, and other employee benefits. Specific benefits and eligibility requirements may vary based on the position and applicable plan provisions. This job posting provides an overview of the role's general nature and expected tasks. It is not meant to be a comprehensive list of all duties performed. The university reserves the right to modify or reassign job responsibilities at any time. This posting description does not constitute an employment contract, either explicit or implied. Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Staff Job Function Finance Pay Type Salary Education Level Bachelor\u2019s Degree Scan this QR code and apply! Download 3135 Easton Turnpike, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA \u00a92009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Cookie Preferences Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"}, "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/shu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/7998": {"title": "Facilities & Construction", "description": "Facilities & Construction - Electrician Lead | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs English (United States) Sign In Facilities & Construction - Electrician Lead Req #925 3135 Easton Turnpike, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA Apply Share Job Description Posted Thursday, October 1, 2026 at 9:00 PM About Sacred Heart University As one of the nation\u2019s largest Catholic universities and among the fastest-growing private doctoral institutions in the U.S., Sacred Heart University is a national leader in shaping higher education for the 21st century. SHU offers more than 100 undergraduate, graduate and doctoral programs on its Fairfield, Conn., campus. Sacred Heart also has a campus in Dingle, Ireland, and offers online programs. Nearly 10,000 students attend the University\u2019s nine colleges and schools: College of Arts & Sciences; School of Communication, Media & the Arts; School of Social Work; School of Computing & Engineering; School of Performing Arts; College of Health Professions; the Isabelle Farrington College of Education & Human Development; the Jack Welch College of Business & Technology; and the Dr. Susan L. Davis, RN, & Richard J. Henley College of Nursing. Sacred Heart, a Laudato Si\u2019 campus, stands out from other Catholic universities as it was established to be led by the laity. This contemporary Catholic university is rooted in the rich Catholic intellectual tradition and the liberal arts and, at the same time, cultivates students to be forward thinkers who enact change in their own lives, professions, and communities.\u202fSacred Heart University has earned national recognition for academic excellence, student success, career outcomes, and campus experience. The Princeton Review recognized SHU in its Best 392 Colleges: 2027 Edition and Best Business Schools: 2027 Edition, while additional national recognitions highlight the University\u2019s commitment to preparing students for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Sacred Heart is home to the award-winning, NPR-affiliate station, WSHU Public Radio; Division I athletics; and an impressive performing arts program that includes choir, band, dance, and theatre . www.sacredheart.edu View SHU\u2019s Faculty Experts Here To apply: Qualified candidates are invited to submit a completed application and r\u00e9sum\u00e9 through the University's online application system. Applications submitted outside of the official Careers at SHU website will not be considered. Applicants should not apply through third-party or external job sites, as such postings may be fraudulent or may misrepresent opportunities that are no longer available at the University. A cover letter or statement of interest is preferred for all staff positions. Sacred Heart University complies with all federal and state employment laws and regulations. Applicants must be lawfully authorized to work for any employer in the United States. We are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa for this position Position Summary The Electrician Lead is responsible for installing, maintaining, troubleshooting, repairing, and inspecting electrical systems and equipment throughout the University's campus. This position supports the safe, reliable, and efficient operation of academic, residential, administrative, athletic, and healthcare facilities. The Electrician Lead performs skilled electrical work in accordance with applicable codes, regulations, and University standards while contributing to preventative maintenance programs, emergency response activities, energy conservation initiatives, and continuous operational improvement efforts. Principal Duties & Responsibilities Install, maintain, troubleshoot, and repair electrical systems and equipment including: Power distribution systems Lighting and lighting controls Emergency power systems Motor controls Variable Frequency Drives (VFDs) Transformers Switchgear and panelboards Fire alarm interfaces Electrical components associated with HVAC and mechanical systems Diagnose electrical issues using testing and diagnostic equipment and implement corrective actions. Perform preventive, predictive, and corrective maintenance on electrical systems and equipment. Install new electrical circuits, conduit, wiring, fixtures, outlets, and equipment as required. Inspect campus facilities and equipment to identify deficiencies, safety concerns, and maintenance needs. Read and interpret: Electrical drawings Blueprints One-line diagrams Schematics Specifications Technical manuals Respond to service requests and emergency calls promptly and professionally. Support campus construction, renovation, and capital improvement projects. Maintain compliance with National Electrical Code (NEC), Connecticut State Electrical Code, OSHA regulations, and University standards. Coordinate work activities with Facilities Operations staff, contractors, vendors, and campus stakeholders. Utilize Computerized Maintenance Management Systems (CMMS) to document work, labor, materials, and equipment history. Assist with operating and maintaining emergency generators and associated transfer switch systems. Participate in on-call rotation as required and respond to after-hours emergencies. Support University sustainability and energy conservation initiatives through efficient operation and optimization of electrical systems. Maintain inventory of electrical materials, tools, and supplies. Perform other tasks assigned by the manager to meet the university's needs. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities & Other Attributes High school diploma or equivalent required; accredited electrical trade school, vocational program, apprenticeship program, or equivalent technical training preferred. Connecticut E-1 Unlimited Electrical Journeyperson License required. Minimum 5 years of commercial, institutional, healthcare, or higher education electrical experience preferred. Strong knowledge of electrical theory, power distribution systems, motor controls, and electrical safety practices. Thorough understanding of the National Electrical Code (NEC) and applicable state and local codes. Experience working with generators, transfer switches, and uninterruptible power supply (UPS) systems preferred. Knowledge of lockout/tagout procedures and electrical safety standards. Familiarity with Building Management Systems (BMS/BAS) preferred. Proficiency with computers, mobile devices, and work order management systems. Ability to work independently and as part of a team. Strong communication and customer service skills. Ability to prioritize multiple tasks in a fast-paced environment. Valid driver's license with an acceptable driving record. Unusual Working Conditions Exposure to energized electrical equipment and circuits while performing testing, troubleshooting, maintenance, and repair activities. Work may be performed in electrical and mechanical rooms, utility tunnels, crawl spaces, above-ceiling areas, confined spaces, rooftops, and other restricted-access areas. Exposure to varying environmental conditions, including heat, cold, humidity, dust, noise, vibration, and inclement weather. Required use of appropriate Personal Protective Equipment (PPE), including arc-flash protective clothing, insulated gloves, safety glasses, hard hats, hearing protection, and other safety equipment as required. Work may involve climbing ladders, scaffolding, and personnel lifts; working at heights; and working around high-voltage electrical distribution equipment, generators, transformers, switchgear, and transfer switches. Must be able to lift, carry, push, and pull electrical equipment, materials, tools, and supplies weighing up to 50 pounds, with assistance for heavier items. Must be available to respond to electrical and life-safety emergencies and participate in an on-call rotation, which may include evenings, weekends, holidays, planned utility shutdowns, and other work outside normal business hours. Must be able to safely perform work in occupied campus facilities while minimizing disruption to University operations. Pre-Employment Requirements All offers of employment are contingent upon satisfactory completion of a background check. In accordance with Connecticut General Statutes \u00a7 31-51v, applicants selected for this position will be required to undergo a pre-employment drug test as a condition of employment. Employment is contingent upon satisfactory results of both the background check and drug test. Compensation & Benefits : The salary range for this position is $40.59 - $48.72 per hour Sacred Heart University offers eligible employees a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, vision, life insurance, disability, retirement, paid time off, and other employee benefits. Specific benefits and eligibility requirements may vary based on the position and applicable plan provisions. This job posting provides an overview of the role's general nature and expected tasks. It is not meant to be a comprehensive list of all duties performed. The university reserves the right to modify or reassign job responsibilities at any time. This posting description does not constitute an employment contract, either explicit or implied. Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Staff Job Function Facilities Pay Type Hourly Scan this QR code and apply! Download 3135 Easton Turnpike, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA \u00a92009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Cookie Preferences Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"}, "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/shu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/7979": {"title": "Facilities & Construction", "description": "Facilities & Construction - Plumber Lead | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs English (United States) Sign In Facilities & Construction - Plumber Lead Req #926 3135 Easton Turnpike, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA Apply Share Job Description Posted Thursday, October 1, 2026 at 9:00 PM About Sacred Heart University As one of the nation\u2019s largest Catholic universities and among the fastest-growing private doctoral institutions in the U.S., Sacred Heart University is a national leader in shaping higher education for the 21st century. SHU offers more than 100 undergraduate, graduate and doctoral programs on its Fairfield, Conn., campus. Sacred Heart also has a campus in Dingle, Ireland, and offers online programs. Nearly 10,000 students attend the University\u2019s nine colleges and schools: College of Arts & Sciences; School of Communication, Media & the Arts; School of Social Work; School of Computing & Engineering; School of Performing Arts; College of Health Professions; the Isabelle Farrington College of Education & Human Development; the Jack Welch College of Business & Technology; and the Dr. Susan L. Davis, RN, & Richard J. Henley College of Nursing. Sacred Heart, a Laudato Si\u2019 campus, stands out from other Catholic universities as it was established to be led by the laity. This contemporary Catholic university is rooted in the rich Catholic intellectual tradition and the liberal arts and, at the same time, cultivates students to be forward thinkers who enact change in their own lives, professions, and communities.\u202fSacred Heart University has earned national recognition for academic excellence, student success, career outcomes, and campus experience. The Princeton Review recognized SHU in its Best 392 Colleges: 2027 Edition and Best Business Schools: 2027 Edition, while additional national recognitions highlight the University\u2019s commitment to preparing students for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Sacred Heart is home to the award-winning, NPR-affiliate station, WSHU Public Radio; Division I athletics; and an impressive performing arts program that includes choir, band, dance, and theatre . www.sacredheart.edu View SHU\u2019s Faculty Experts Here To apply: Qualified candidates are invited to submit a completed application and r\u00e9sum\u00e9 through the University's online application system. Applications submitted outside of the official Careers at SHU website will not be considered. Applicants should not apply through third-party or external job sites, as such postings may be fraudulent or may misrepresent opportunities that are no longer available at the University. A cover letter or statement of interest is preferred for all staff positions. Sacred Heart University complies with all federal and state employment laws and regulations. Applicants must be lawfully authorized to work for any employer in the United States. We are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa for this position Position Summary The Plumber Lead is responsible for installing, maintaining, repairing, inspecting, and operating plumbing, piping, drainage, water distribution, sanitary sewer, and related mechanical systems throughout Sacred Heart University's campus. The position ensures that all plumbing systems operate safely, efficiently, and in compliance with applicable local, state, and federal codes while supporting the University's commitment to providing a safe, comfortable, and reliable environment for students, faculty, staff, and visitors. The Plumber Lead performs preventive and corrective maintenance, responds to emergency service calls, assists with renovation and construction projects, and collaborates with other Facilities personnel to maintain campus infrastructure and support institutional objectives. Principal Duties & Responsibilities Maintains and repairs plumbing systems serving academic buildings, residence halls, athletic facilities, dining facilities, laboratories, administrative offices, and campus support buildings. Responsible for diagnosing and resolving issues involving domestic water, sanitary waste, storm drainage, natural gas piping, pumps, fixtures, valves, water heaters, backflow prevention devices, and related equipment. Performs preventative maintenance inspections to maximize system reliability and reduce operational disruptions. Responds to emergency situations including leaks, pipe failures, sewer backups, water quality concerns, and equipment malfunctions. Supports campus renovation and capital improvement projects by reviewing plans, installing piping systems, coordinating utility shutdowns, and ensuring code compliance. Documents work performed, labor hours, materials used, and equipment history. Works independently with minimal supervision while coordinating with Facilities, Public Safety, contractors, vendors, and project managers. May provide technical guidance and mentoring to maintenance technicians, apprentices, and other Facilities personnel. Participates in an on-call rotation and may be required to work evenings, weekends, holidays, and during campus emergencies. Thorough knowledge of plumbing principles, practices, materials, methods, and tools. Comprehensive understanding of Connecticut State Plumbing Codes, building codes, health regulations, and safety standards. Understanding of plumbing-related mechanical equipment including pumps, water heaters, pressure-reducing stations, expansion systems, and water treatment components. Familiarity with blueprint reading, schematics, specifications, and construction documents. Perform other tasks assigned by the manager in response to the needs of the university. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities & Other Attributes Connecticut P-2 or P-1 Plumbing License required. High school diploma or GED required; completion of an accredited HVAC technical school program, trade school certificate, or equivalent vocational training preferred. Minimum of five (5) years of progressively responsible plumbing experience in commercial, institutional, healthcare, higher education, or industrial facilities. Valid driver's license with an acceptable driving record. Backflow Prevention Certification. OSHA 10 or OSHA 30 certification. Knowledge of steam, hydronic, and mechanical building systems. Experience supporting renovation and construction projects. Ability to install, repair, maintain, and test plumbing systems and components. Skilled in diagnosing system failures and determining effective corrective actions. Proficient in pipe fitting, soldering, brazing, threading, welding coordination, and fixture installation. Ability to perform inspections and compliance testing of plumbing systems. Competence in operating plumbing equipment, drain-cleaning machines, pipe threading equipment, leak detection devices, and testing instruments. Unusual Working Conditions Works in a variety of indoor and outdoor environments under varying weather conditions, including extreme heat, cold, rain, snow, and humidity. Regularly works in confined spaces, crawl spaces, tunnels, utility vaults, mechanical rooms, construction areas, and other restricted-access locations. May be exposed to wastewater, sewage systems, domestic water systems, chemical treatment equipment, dust, dirt, odors, noise, vibration, and potentially unsanitary conditions. May be exposed to cleaning agents, solvents, adhesives, fluxes, fuels, and other chemicals associated with plumbing and maintenance operations. Performs physically demanding work requiring prolonged standing and walking; climbing ladders, scaffolding, lifts, and stairs; and frequent bending, kneeling, crouching, reaching, and working in awkward positions. Regularly lifts, carries, pushes, and pulls tools, equipment, materials, and piping components weighing up to 50 pounds independently, with assistance or mechanical lifting devices used for heavier items. May work around energized mechanical equipment, pressurized piping, natural gas systems, hot water systems, and steam-related infrastructure. Required to wear appropriate Personal Protective Equipment (PPE), including safety glasses, gloves, hearing protection, protective footwear, respirators, and other safety equipment as required. Must be available to respond to emergency service calls and participate in an on-call rotation, which may include evenings, weekends, holidays, severe weather events, and other emergency campus operations. May be required to perform or support planned utility shutdowns outside normal business hours to minimize disruption to University operations. Pre-Employment Requirements All offers of employment are contingent upon satisfactory completion of a background check. In accordance with Connecticut General Statutes \u00a7 31-51v, applicants selected for this position will be required to undergo a pre-employment drug test as a condition of employment. Employment is contingent upon satisfactory results of both the background check and drug test. Compensation & Benefits : The salary range for this position is $39.82 - $49.75 per hour Sacred Heart University offers eligible employees a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, vision, life insurance, disability, retirement, paid time off, and other employee benefits. Specific benefits and eligibility requirements may vary based on the position and applicable plan provisions. This job posting provides an overview of the role's general nature and expected tasks. It is not meant to be a comprehensive list of all duties performed. The university reserves the right to modify or reassign job responsibilities at any time. This posting description does not constitute an employment contract, either explicit or implied. Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Staff Pay Type Hourly Scan this QR code and apply! Download 3135 Easton Turnpike, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA \u00a92009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Cookie Preferences Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"}, "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/shu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/7975": {"title": "Facilities & Construction", "description": "Facilities & Construction - HVAC Lead | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs English (United States) Sign In Facilities & Construction - HVAC Lead Req #927 3135 Easton Turnpike, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA Apply Share Job Description Posted Thursday, October 1, 2026 at 9:00 PM About Sacred Heart University As one of the nation\u2019s largest Catholic universities and among the fastest-growing private doctoral institutions in the U.S., Sacred Heart University is a national leader in shaping higher education for the 21st century. SHU offers more than 100 undergraduate, graduate and doctoral programs on its Fairfield, Conn., campus. Sacred Heart also has a campus in Dingle, Ireland, and offers online programs. Nearly 10,000 students attend the University\u2019s nine colleges and schools: College of Arts & Sciences; School of Communication, Media & the Arts; School of Social Work; School of Computing & Engineering; School of Performing Arts; College of Health Professions; the Isabelle Farrington College of Education & Human Development; the Jack Welch College of Business & Technology; and the Dr. Susan L. Davis, RN, & Richard J. Henley College of Nursing. Sacred Heart, a Laudato Si\u2019 campus, stands out from other Catholic universities as it was established to be led by the laity. This contemporary Catholic university is rooted in the rich Catholic intellectual tradition and the liberal arts and, at the same time, cultivates students to be forward thinkers who enact change in their own lives, professions, and communities.\u202fSacred Heart University has earned national recognition for academic excellence, student success, career outcomes, and campus experience. The Princeton Review recognized SHU in its Best 392 Colleges: 2027 Edition and Best Business Schools: 2027 Edition, while additional national recognitions highlight the University\u2019s commitment to preparing students for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Sacred Heart is home to the award-winning, NPR-affiliate station, WSHU Public Radio; Division I athletics; and an impressive performing arts program that includes choir, band, dance, and theatre . www.sacredheart.edu View SHU\u2019s Faculty Experts Here To apply: Qualified candidates are invited to submit a completed application and r\u00e9sum\u00e9 through the University's online application system. Applications submitted outside of the official Careers at SHU website will not be considered. Applicants should not apply through third-party or external job sites, as such postings may be fraudulent or may misrepresent opportunities that are no longer available at the University. A cover letter or statement of interest is preferred for all staff positions. Sacred Heart University complies with all federal and state employment laws and regulations. Applicants must be lawfully authorized to work for any employer in the United States. We are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa for this position Position Summary The HVAC Lead is responsible for installing, maintaining, troubleshooting, repairing, and operating HVAC, refrigeration, and Building Management Systems throughout Sacred Heart University's facilities. Ensures campus mechanical systems operate safely, efficiently, and reliably while supporting occupant comfort, energy management initiatives, and the University's commitment to providing an exceptional learning, living, and working environment. Principal Duties & Responsibilities Maintain, diagnose, troubleshoot, repair, and install commercial HVAC equipment and systems, including: chillers, boilers, Air Handling Units (AHUs), Rooftop Units (RTUs), Variable Air Volume (VAV) systems, heat pumps, exhaust and supply fans, split systems, and Variable Refrigerant Flow (VRF) systems. Monitor, operate, and adjust HVAC system performance through the University\u2019s Building Management System (BMS). Troubleshoot HVAC controls and Building Automation Systems (BAS/BMS), including sensors, actuators, valves, Variable Frequency Drives (VFDs), and associated control devices. Perform preventive maintenance on HVAC and mechanical equipment to maximize system reliability, efficiency, and lifespan. Respond to service calls, maintenance requests, and work orders in a timely and professional manner. Assist with the commissioning, startup, testing, and performance verification of HVAC systems and building controls. Maintain accurate records of maintenance activities, work orders, equipment repairs, inspections, and testing. Coordinate with contractors, vendors, and Facilities Management personnel regarding maintenance activities, repairs, and capital projects. Participate in after-hours emergency response and on-call rotation as required to support campus operations. Ensure compliance with all applicable safety regulations, University policies, licensing requirements, codes, and industry standards. Train and mentor maintenance personnel, helpers, and apprentices as assigned. Safeguard University-owned tools, equipment, materials, and vehicles from loss, theft, misuse, or damage. Assist technicians in other trades and specialties as needed, provided all life safety requirements, licensing regulations, and applicable codes are maintained. Support the University\u2019s commitment to providing a safe, comfortable, and energy-efficient campus environment. Perform other duties as assigned by the Manager in response to the needs of the University. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities, & Other Attributes High school diploma or completion of an accredited HVAC technical school program, trade school certificate, or equivalent vocational training preferred. Connecticut S-1 Unlimited Heating, Piping, and Cooling Journeyperson License is highly preferred. Minimum 5 years of commercial, institutional, healthcare, or higher education HVAC experience. Strong understanding of HVAC mechanical systems, refrigeration cycles, and controls. Experience with Building Management Systems (BMS/BAS) is highly preferred Ability to read and interpret: Mechanical Drawings, Control Schematics, Blueprints, Technical Manuals Working knowledge of electrical troubleshooting related to HVAC equipment. EPA Universal Refrigerant Certification preferred. Proficiency with computers, mobile devices, and work order management systems. Valid driver's license with a clean driving record. Unusual Working Conditions Works in a variety of indoor and outdoor environments and may be exposed to extreme temperatures, inclement weather, noise, vibration, dust, odors, and other conditions associated with mechanical and maintenance operations. Work may be performed in confined or restricted-access areas, including crawl spaces, tunnels, utility vaults, and mechanical rooms, and may require climbing ladders, scaffolding, lifts, and stairs. Performs physically demanding work involving prolonged standing, walking, bending, kneeling, crouching, reaching, and lifting or moving equipment and materials weighing up to 50 pounds independently and heavier items with assistance or mechanical lifting devices. Required to wear appropriate personal protective equipment (PPE) and follow all applicable safety procedures. Participates in an on-call rotation and may be required to work evenings, weekends, holidays, severe weather events, or other emergency situations, including equipment failures, utility interruptions, and planned utility shutdowns. Pre-Employment Requirements All offers of employment are contingent upon satisfactory completion of a background check. In accordance with Connecticut General Statutes \u00a7 31-51v, applicants selected for this position will be required to undergo a pre-employment drug test as a condition of employment. Employment is contingent upon satisfactory results of both the background check and drug test. Compensation & Benefits : The salary range for this position is $38.25 - $46.04 per hour Sacred Heart University offers eligible employees a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, vision, life insurance, disability, retirement, paid time off, and other employee benefits. Specific benefits and eligibility requirements may vary based on the position and applicable plan provisions. This job posting provides an overview of the role's general nature and expected tasks. It is not meant to be a comprehensive list of all duties performed. The university reserves the right to modify or reassign job responsibilities at any time. This posting description does not constitute an employment contract, either explicit or implied. Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Staff Job Function Facilities Pay Type Hourly Scan this QR code and apply! Download 3135 Easton Turnpike, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA \u00a92009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Cookie Preferences Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"}, "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/shu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/7960": {"title": "Facilities & Construction", "description": "Facilities & Construction - HVAC Journeyman | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs English (United States) Sign In Facilities & Construction - HVAC Journeyman Req #928 3135 Easton Turnpike, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA Apply Share Job Description Posted Thursday, October 1, 2026 at 9:00 PM About Sacred Heart University As one of the nation\u2019s largest Catholic universities and among the fastest-growing private doctoral institutions in the U.S., Sacred Heart University is a national leader in shaping higher education for the 21st century. SHU offers more than 100 undergraduate, graduate and doctoral programs on its Fairfield, Conn., campus. Sacred Heart also has a campus in Dingle, Ireland, and offers online programs. Nearly 10,000 students attend the University\u2019s nine colleges and schools: College of Arts & Sciences; School of Communication, Media & the Arts; School of Social Work; School of Computing & Engineering; School of Performing Arts; College of Health Professions; the Isabelle Farrington College of Education & Human Development; the Jack Welch College of Business & Technology; and the Dr. Susan L. Davis, RN, & Richard J. Henley College of Nursing. Sacred Heart, a Laudato Si\u2019 campus, stands out from other Catholic universities as it was established to be led by the laity. This contemporary Catholic university is rooted in the rich Catholic intellectual tradition and the liberal arts and, at the same time, cultivates students to be forward thinkers who enact change in their own lives, professions, and communities.\u202fSacred Heart University has earned national recognition for academic excellence, student success, career outcomes, and campus experience. The Princeton Review recognized SHU in its Best 392 Colleges: 2027 Edition and Best Business Schools: 2027 Edition, while additional national recognitions highlight the University\u2019s commitment to preparing students for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Sacred Heart is home to the award-winning, NPR-affiliate station, WSHU Public Radio; Division I athletics; and an impressive performing arts program that includes choir, band, dance, and theatre . www.sacredheart.edu View SHU\u2019s Faculty Experts Here To apply: Qualified candidates are invited to submit a completed application and r\u00e9sum\u00e9 through the University's online application system. Applications submitted outside of the official Careers at SHU website will not be considered. Applicants should not apply through third-party or external job sites, as such postings may be fraudulent or may misrepresent opportunities that are no longer available at the University. A cover letter or statement of interest is preferred for all staff positions. Sacred Heart University complies with all federal and state employment laws and regulations. Applicants must be lawfully authorized to work for any employer in the United States. We are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa for this position Position Summary Perform skilled journeyman-level work in the heating, ventilation, and air conditioning (HVAC) trade in support of the maintenance, repair, troubleshooting, installation, alteration, and preventive maintenance of University buildings, facilities, and mechanical systems. Independently diagnose and resolve HVAC-related issues; maintain and service HVAC equipment and associated controls; support the operation of building management and energy management systems; and ensure work is completed safely, efficiently, and in accordance with applicable codes, regulations, manufacturer specifications, and University standards. Collaborate with Facilities & Construction staff, other skilled trades, contractors, and University departments to support reliable building operations, occupant comfort, energy efficiency, and timely completion of maintenance and capital projects. Principal Duties & Responsibilities Perform skilled journeyman-level HVAC work across University facilities, including the inspection, installation, maintenance, troubleshooting, repair, replacement, and alteration of HVAC equipment, systems, and related components. Complete assigned work orders accurately, safely, efficiently, and within established priorities and timelines. Diagnose and troubleshoot mechanical, electrical, refrigeration, and control-related issues within the employee\u2019s training, licensing, and authorization. Perform scheduled preventive maintenance in accordance with established procedures, manufacturer recommendations, applicable codes, and University standards. Inspect HVAC equipment, systems, and campus facilities to identify required repairs, maintenance needs, safety concerns, and potential equipment failures. Use appropriate diagnostic tools, testing equipment, technical documentation, and sound judgment to evaluate system performance and identify the cause of equipment or system problems. Install, replace, adjust, and maintain HVAC equipment, components, controls, and related systems as assigned. Maintain, monitor, and troubleshoot automated building management and energy management systems and controls. Read and interpret blueprints, schematics, equipment manuals, diagrams, and technical instructions. Perform all work in accordance with applicable federal, state, and local laws, codes, licensing requirements, safety standards, manufacturer specifications, and University policies. Maintain all required licenses, certifications, registrations, and professional credentials applicable to assigned responsibilities. Maintain accurate work order documentation, including work performed, materials used, equipment conditions, identified issues, and recommended follow-up. Identify and communicate material, equipment, and service needs to the Manager, Maintenance & Trades. Assist with estimating materials, preparing requisition information, and coordinating the procurement of equipment or services as requested. Recommend equipment repairs, replacements, and system improvements based on equipment condition, operational requirements, lifecycle considerations, energy conservation, and cost effectiveness. Participate in the planning, coordination, and completion of in-house capital projects, renovations, equipment installations, and HVAC system upgrades. Coordinate work with other skilled trades, Facilities & Construction personnel, contractors, and University departments to support safe, efficient, and timely completion of assignments. Assist with the coordination and review of contracted HVAC services, including providing technical information and verifying work as requested. Provide technical guidance, instruction, and training to HVAC technicians, helpers, apprentices, or other employees as directed. Such responsibilities do not constitute formal supervisory authority unless specifically assigned. Use University tools, equipment, materials, and resources appropriately, and safeguard them from damage, loss, misuse, or theft. Assist other trades and Campus Operations personnel as needed, provided that applicable safety, licensing, and regulatory requirements are maintained. Respond to after-hours emergency calls and urgent Campus Operations requests as assigned. Participate in ongoing professional development, safety training, and advancements in HVAC technology, equipment, and controls. Assist with snow removal and other operational needs as assigned. Perform all other related duties as assigned by management in response to the needs of the University Knowledge, Skills, Abilities, & Other Attributes High school diploma or equivalent required. Completion of a recognized HVAC/R apprenticeship, technical training program, or equivalent combination of education and experience preferred. Current Connecticut journeyman-level HVAC, refrigeration, or related trade license appropriate to the position and assigned duties required. Current S-2 license is required, if applicable to the work performed. Minimum of three years of journeyman-level HVAC experience in a commercial, institutional, or similar environment required. Demonstrated knowledge and experience in the installation, maintenance, troubleshooting, repair, and operation of commercial HVAC systems and related equipment required. Working knowledge of refrigeration systems, electrical components, motors, pumps, controls, air-handling equipment, boilers, chillers, rooftop units, and related mechanical systems required or preferred based on assigned responsibilities. Ability to independently diagnose HVAC system and equipment problems using appropriate tools, testing equipment, schematics, manuals, and technical documentation required. Knowledge of building management systems (BMS) and energy management controls preferred. Ability to read and interpret blueprints, schematics, equipment manuals, diagrams, and technical instructions required. Knowledge of applicable HVAC codes, licensing requirements, safety standards, environmental regulations, and University policies required. Ability to use computerized work order systems, email, and other technology necessary to document and complete work required. Ability to work independently, prioritize assignments, exercise sound technical judgment, and communicate work status, issues, and recommended follow-up required. Ability to work effectively and cooperatively with other skilled trades, supervisors, contractors, vendors, and University departments required. Ability to provide technical guidance, instruction, and training to HVAC technicians, helpers, apprentices, or other employees as directed required. Strong troubleshooting, problem-solving, communication, organizational, and customer service skills required. Commitment to maintaining required licenses and certifications and participating in ongoing professional and technical development required. A current, valid Connecticut driver\u2019s license with a clean driving record is required. Unusual Working Conditions Work involves frequent exposure to dust, dirt, fumes, heat, cold, potentially hazardous chemicals, mechanical and electrical conditions, and working at heights or in confined and cramped areas. Regular use of hand tools, power tools, testing equipment, ladders, lifts, and machinery is required. The position requires the ability to lift and carry a minimum of 40 pounds, as well as the physical ability to stand, walk, bend, kneel, climb, reach, and work in various building and mechanical environments. May be required to work flexible hours, evenings, weekends, holidays, or respond to after-hours emergencies and urgent Campus Operations requests. May assist with snow removal and other operational needs as assigned. Pre-Employment Requirements All offers of employment are contingent upon satisfactory completion of a background check. In accordance with Connecticut General Statutes \u00a7 31-51v, applicants selected for this position will be required to undergo a pre-employment drug test as a condition of employment. Employment is contingent upon satisfactory results of both the background check and drug test. Compensation & Benefits : The salary range for this position is $34.34 - $42.19 per hour Sacred Heart University offers eligible employees a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, vision, life insurance, disability, retirement, paid time off, and other employee benefits. Specific benefits and eligibility requirements may vary based on the position and applicable plan provisions. This job posting provides an overview of the role's general nature and expected tasks. It is not meant to be a comprehensive list of all duties performed. The university reserves the right to modify or reassign job responsibilities at any time. This posting description does not constitute an employment contract, either explicit or implied. Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Staff Job Function Facilities Pay Type Hourly Scan this QR code and apply! Download 3135 Easton Turnpike, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA \u00a92009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Cookie Preferences Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"}, "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/shu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/7901": {"title": "Physics - Adjunct Instructor (Ongoing)", "description": "Physics - Adjunct Instructor (Ongoing) | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs English (United States) Sign In Physics - Adjunct Instructor (Ongoing) Req #208 5151 Park Ave, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA Apply Share Job Description Posted Wednesday, September 30, 2026 at 9:00 PM About Sacred Heart University As one of the nation\u2019s largest Catholic universities and among the fastest-growing private doctoral institutions in the U.S., Sacred Heart University is a national leader in shaping higher education for the 21st century. SHU offers more than 100 undergraduate, graduate and doctoral programs on its Fairfield, Conn., campus. Sacred Heart also has a campus in Dingle, Ireland, and offers online programs. Nearly 10,000 students attend the University\u2019s nine colleges and schools: College of Arts & Sciences; School of Communication, Media & the Arts; School of Social Work; School of Computing & Engineering; School of Performing Arts; College of Health Professions; the Isabelle Farrington College of Education & Human Development; the Jack Welch College of Business & Technology; and the Dr. Susan L. Davis, RN, & Richard J. Henley College of Nursing. Sacred Heart, a Laudato Si\u2019 campus, stands out from other Catholic universities as it was established to be led by the laity. This contemporary Catholic university is rooted in the rich Catholic intellectual tradition and the liberal arts and, at the same time, cultivates students to be forward thinkers who enact change in their own lives, professions, and communities.\u202fSacred Heart University has earned national recognition for academic excellence, student success, career outcomes, and campus experience. The Princeton Review recognized SHU in its Best 392 Colleges: 2027 Edition and Best Business Schools: 2027 Edition, while additional national recognitions highlight the University\u2019s commitment to preparing students for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Sacred Heart is home to the award-winning, NPR-affiliate station, WSHU Public Radio; Division I athletics; and an impressive performing arts program that includes choir, band, dance, and theatre. www.sacredheart.edu View SHU\u2019s Faculty Experts Here Sacred Heart University\u2019s Department of Chemistry & Physics in the College of Arts & Sciences invites applications for Adjunct Instructors who can make the principles governing motion, energy, sound, light, and matter tangible through rigorous, hands-on instruction. This is an opportunity to bring scientific expertise into classroom and laboratory experiences that strengthen quantitative reasoning, experimental judgment, and a deeper understanding of the physical world. Teaching opportunities span introductory lectures and laboratories in mechanics, thermodynamics, waves, sound, electricity, magnetism, optics, and modern physics. Algebra- and calculus-based courses serve students across the sciences, health professions, speech-language pathology, and education, allowing instructors to connect foundational theory with the distinct questions and applications of each field. Potential teaching assignments are outlined in the Chemistry & Physics course descriptions . Requirements: Master\u2019s degree or Ph.D. in Physics, Engineering, or a closely related field Demonstrated college-level teaching experience Commitment to fostering a collegial and supportive learning environment that reflects the University\u2019s mission and values Application Instructions: Qualified applicants are invited to submit a letter of interest, current CV, statement of teaching philosophy, and relevant examples from courses taught (if applicable). Upon offer of employment, the selected candidate will be required to provide one formal letter of recommendation on professional letterhead and an official transcript reflecting their highest earned degree. Applications will be reviewed on an ongoing basis based on the needs of the department. Questions regarding this opportunity may be directed to Dr. Samah Senbel. Compensation & Benefits: The salary range for this position is\u00a0$4,300\u2013$5,400 per 3-credit course. Adjunct Instructors are not eligible to participate in the University\u2019s employee health and welfare benefit programs; however, they are eligible to participate in Sacred Heart University\u2019s 403(b) retirement plan, subject to the terms and eligibility requirements of the plan. Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Faculty Job Function Faculty Pay Type Salary Education Level Master\u2019s Degree Scan this QR code and apply! Download 5151 Park Ave, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA \u00a92009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Cookie Preferences Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"}, "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/shu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/7890": {"title": "Radiography - Adjunct Instructor", "description": "Radiography - Adjunct Instructor | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs English (United States) Sign In Radiography - Adjunct Instructor Req #233 4000 Park Ave, Bridgeport, CT 06604, USA Apply Share Job Description Posted Wednesday, September 30, 2026 at 9:00 PM About Sacred Heart University As one of the nation\u2019s largest Catholic universities and among the fastest-growing private doctoral institutions in the U.S., Sacred Heart University is a national leader in shaping higher education for the 21st century. SHU offers more than 100 undergraduate, graduate and doctoral programs on its Fairfield, Conn., campus. Sacred Heart also has a campus in Dingle, Ireland, and offers online programs. Nearly 10,000 students attend the University\u2019s nine colleges and schools: College of Arts & Sciences; School of Communication, Media & the Arts; School of Social Work; School of Computing & Engineering; School of Performing Arts; College of Health Professions; the Isabelle Farrington College of Education & Human Development; the Jack Welch College of Business & Technology; and the Dr. Susan L. Davis, RN, & Richard J. Henley College of Nursing. Sacred Heart, a Laudato Si\u2019 campus, stands out from other Catholic universities as it was established to be led by the laity. This contemporary Catholic university is rooted in the rich Catholic intellectual tradition and the liberal arts and, at the same time, cultivates students to be forward thinkers who enact change in their own lives, professions, and communities.\u202fSacred Heart University has earned national recognition for academic excellence, student success, career outcomes, and campus experience. The Princeton Review recognized SHU in its Best 392 Colleges: 2027 Edition and Best Business Schools: 2027 Edition, while additional national recognitions highlight the University\u2019s commitment to preparing students for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Sacred Heart is home to the award-winning, NPR-affiliate station, WSHU Public Radio; Division I athletics; and an impressive performing arts program that includes choir, band, dance, and theatre. www.sacredheart.edu View SHU\u2019s Faculty Experts Here Sacred Heart University\u2019s College of Health Professions invites applications for part-time adjunct faculty to support the Associate of Science in Radiography program as instructional needs arise. The Radiography program prepares students for entry-level practice in the medical imaging field through a curriculum that combines foundational sciences, radiologic sciences, and patient care. Coursework includes areas such as image production and acquisition, equipment operation, quality control, radiation protection, digital imaging, and specialized imaging modalities. Responsibilities: Teach assigned didactic courses in on-ground and/or online formats. Develop and facilitate instructional content and assess student learning. Use a variety of instructional strategies to engage students and support learning outcomes. Utilize Blackboard Ultra to manage course materials and communication. Provide regular and timely feedback to students and be available for student support. Advise students on matters related to academics, clinical progress, attendance, and professional expectations. Maintain and report grades and attendance in accordance with University policies. Requirements: Bachelor\u2019s degree preferred. Current ARRT\u00ae certification and registration in Radiography (R); additional credentials in Computed Tomography (CT), Magnetic Resonance (MR), and/or Mammography (M) are preferred. Current State of Connecticut Radiographer license. Minimum of two years of professional experience. Prior college-level teaching experience and proficiency with an online course management system are preferred. Application Instructions: Qualified applicants are invited to submit a letter of interest, current CV, statement of teaching philosophy, and relevant examples from courses taught (if applicable). Upon offer of employment, the selected candidate will be required to provide one formal letter of recommendation on professional letterhead and an official transcript reflecting their highest earned degree. Please apply online via this portal. Faxes and emails will not be accepted. Compensation & Benefits: The salary range for this position is\u00a0$4,300\u2013$5,400 per 3-credit course. Adjunct Instructors are not eligible to participate in the University\u2019s employee health and welfare benefit programs; however, they are eligible to participate in Sacred Heart University\u2019s 403(b) retirement plan, subject to the terms and eligibility requirements of the plan. Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Faculty Job Function Faculty Pay Type Salary Education Level Bachelor\u2019s Degree Scan this QR code and apply! Download 4000 Park Ave, Bridgeport, CT 06604, USA \u00a92009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Cookie Preferences Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"}, "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/shu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/7835": {"title": "Adjunct Instructor", "description": "Adjunct Instructor - Economics, Welch College of Business & Technology (Ongoing) | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs English (United States) Sign In Adjunct Instructor - Economics, Welch College of Business & Technology (Ongoing) Req #108 3135 Easton Turnpike, Fairfield, Connecticut, United States of America Apply Share Job Description Posted Wednesday, September 30, 2026 at 9:00 PM About Sacred Heart University As one of the nation\u2019s largest Catholic universities and among the fastest-growing private doctoral institutions in the U.S., Sacred Heart University is a national leader in shaping higher education for the 21st century. SHU offers more than 100 undergraduate, graduate and doctoral programs on its Fairfield, Conn., campus. Sacred Heart also has a campus in Dingle, Ireland, and offers online programs. Nearly 10,000 students attend the University\u2019s nine colleges and schools: College of Arts & Sciences; School of Communication, Media & the Arts; School of Social Work; School of Computing & Engineering; School of Performing Arts; College of Health Professions; the Isabelle Farrington College of Education & Human Development; the Jack Welch College of Business & Technology; and the Dr. Susan L. Davis, RN, & Richard J. Henley College of Nursing. Sacred Heart, a Laudato Si\u2019 campus, stands out from other Catholic universities as it was established to be led by the laity. This contemporary Catholic university is rooted in the rich Catholic intellectual tradition and the liberal arts and, at the same time, cultivates students to be forward thinkers who enact change in their own lives, professions, and communities.\u202fSacred Heart University has earned national recognition for academic excellence, student success, career outcomes, and campus experience. The Princeton Review recognized SHU in its Best 392 Colleges: 2027 Edition and Best Business Schools: 2027 Edition, while additional national recognitions highlight the University\u2019s commitment to preparing students for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Sacred Heart is home to the award-winning, NPR-affiliate station, WSHU Public Radio; Division I athletics; and an impressive performing arts program that includes choir, band, dance, and theatre. www.sacredheart.edu View SHU\u2019s Faculty Experts Here Sacred Heart University\u2019s Economics Department in the Welch College of Business & Technology invites applications for Adjunct Instructors committed to engaging students in the study of economic theory, global economic trends, and business decision-making. Sacred Heart\u2019s economics programs bring economic theory to life through practical business applications and the examination of current global issues. Adjunct instructors have the opportunity to bring their academic and professional expertise into the classroom while helping students develop the analytical and problem-solving skills needed to evaluate complex economic issues and understand how markets, public policy, and global forces influence business decisions. Current undergraduate offerings include: Bachelor of Science in Business Economics Minor in Economics Responsibilities: Teach assigned undergraduate economics courses in accordance with established course objectives and academic standards Create an engaging and supportive learning environment Provide students with timely feedback and maintain regular communication throughout the course Collaborate with the department chair and faculty as appropriate Fulfill all responsibilities associated with the assigned course Requirements: A minimum of a master\u2019s degree in economics or a closely related field A terminal degree is preferred Prior college-level teaching experience is preferred Strong verbal, written, organizational, and interpersonal skills Commitment to fostering a collegial and supportive environment in which all members of the University community can thrive and succeed Application Instructions: Qualified applicants are invited to submit a letter of interest, current CV, statement of teaching philosophy, and relevant examples from courses taught (if applicable). Upon offer of employment, the selected candidate will be required to provide one formal letter of recommendation on professional letterhead and an official transcript reflecting their highest earned degree. Compensation & Benefits: The salary range for this position is\u00a0$4,300\u2013$5,400 per 3-credit course. Adjunct Instructors are not eligible to participate in the University\u2019s employee health and welfare benefit programs; however, they are eligible to participate in Sacred Heart University\u2019s 403(b) retirement plan, subject to the terms and eligibility requirements of the plan. Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Faculty Job Function Faculty Pay Type Salary Education Level Master\u2019s Degree Scan this QR code and apply! Download 3135 Easton Turnpike, Fairfield, Connecticut, United States of America \u00a92009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Cookie Preferences Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"}, "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/shu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/7823": {"title": "Adjunct Instructor", "description": "Adjunct Instructor - Management, Welch College of Business & Technology (Ongoing) | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs English (United States) Sign In Adjunct Instructor - Management, Welch College of Business & Technology (Ongoing) Req #61 3135 Easton Turnpike, Fairfield, Connecticut, United States of America Apply Share Job Description Posted Wednesday, September 30, 2026 at 9:00 PM About Sacred Heart University As one of the nation\u2019s largest Catholic universities and among the fastest-growing private doctoral institutions in the U.S., Sacred Heart University is a national leader in shaping higher education for the 21st century. SHU offers more than 100 undergraduate, graduate and doctoral programs on its Fairfield, Conn., campus. Sacred Heart also has a campus in Dingle, Ireland, and offers online programs. Nearly 10,000 students attend the University\u2019s nine colleges and schools: College of Arts & Sciences; School of Communication, Media & the Arts; School of Social Work; School of Computing & Engineering; School of Performing Arts; College of Health Professions; the Isabelle Farrington College of Education & Human Development; the Jack Welch College of Business & Technology; and the Dr. Susan L. Davis, RN, & Richard J. Henley College of Nursing. Sacred Heart, a Laudato Si\u2019 campus, stands out from other Catholic universities as it was established to be led by the laity. This contemporary Catholic university is rooted in the rich Catholic intellectual tradition and the liberal arts and, at the same time, cultivates students to be forward thinkers who enact change in their own lives, professions, and communities.\u202fSacred Heart University has earned national recognition for academic excellence, student success, career outcomes, and campus experience. The Princeton Review recognized SHU in its Best 392 Colleges: 2027 Edition and Best Business Schools: 2027 Edition, while additional national recognitions highlight the University\u2019s commitment to preparing students for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Sacred Heart is home to the award-winning, NPR-affiliate station, WSHU Public Radio; Division I athletics; and an impressive performing arts program that includes choir, band, dance, and theatre. www.sacredheart.edu View SHU\u2019s Faculty Experts Here Sacred Heart University\u2019s Department of Management in the AACSB-accredited Welch College of Business & Technology invites applications for Adjunct Instructors committed to developing mindful, innovative leaders prepared to strengthen organizations and make a positive impact on business and society. Adjunct instructors join an interdisciplinary community of accomplished scholars and seasoned practitioners with expertise spanning strategy, organizational behavior, entrepreneurship, innovation, human resource management, operations, supply chain management, business law, and international management. Drawing on academic and professional experience, instructors create active and engaging learning experiences where students apply established frameworks to real organizational challenges and strengthen the judgment, leadership, teamwork, and ethical decision-making skills needed in a changing global landscape. Management offers undergraduate and graduate programs, including a Bachelor of Science in Management, an MBA, and specialized minors and graduate certificates. Additional information about available classes can be found in the Management course descriptions . Responsibilities: Teach assigned undergraduate or graduate management courses in accordance with established course objectives and academic standards Create an active, engaging, and supportive learning environment Connect management concepts and established frameworks with relevant organizational and business challenges Provide students with timely feedback and maintain regular communication throughout the course Collaborate with the department chair and faculty as appropriate Fulfill all responsibilities associated with the assigned course Qualifications: A minimum of a master\u2019s degree in management, business, or a closely related field Academic or professional expertise relevant to the assigned course Prior college-level teaching experience is preferred Strong verbal, written, organizational, and interpersonal skills Commitment to fostering a collegial and supportive environment in which all members of the University community can thrive and succeed Application Instructions: Qualified applicants are invited to submit a letter of interest, current CV, statement of teaching philosophy, and relevant examples from courses taught (if applicable). Upon offer of employment, the selected candidate will be required to provide one formal letter of recommendation on professional letterhead and an official transcript reflecting their highest earned degree. Review of applications will be ongoing based on the needs of the department. Compensation & Benefits: The salary range for this position is\u00a0$4,300\u2013$5,400 per 3-credit course. Adjunct Instructors are not eligible to participate in the University\u2019s employee health and welfare benefit programs; however, they are eligible to participate in Sacred Heart University\u2019s 403(b) retirement plan, subject to the terms and eligibility requirements of the plan. Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Faculty Job Function Faculty Pay Type Salary Education Level Master\u2019s Degree Scan this QR code and apply! Download 3135 Easton Turnpike, Fairfield, Connecticut, United States of America \u00a92009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Cookie Preferences Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"}, "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/shu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/7757": {"title": "Adjunct Instructor", "description": "Adjunct Instructor - Marketing, Welch College of Business & Technology (Ongoing) | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs English (United States) Sign In Adjunct Instructor - Marketing, Welch College of Business & Technology (Ongoing) Req #410 3135 Easton Turnpike, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA Apply Share Job Description Posted Wednesday, September 30, 2026 at 9:00 PM About Sacred Heart University As one of the nation\u2019s largest Catholic universities and among the fastest-growing private doctoral institutions in the U.S., Sacred Heart University is a national leader in shaping higher education for the 21st century. SHU offers more than 100 undergraduate, graduate and doctoral programs on its Fairfield, Conn., campus. Sacred Heart also has a campus in Dingle, Ireland, and offers online programs. Nearly 10,000 students attend the University\u2019s nine colleges and schools: College of Arts & Sciences; School of Communication, Media & the Arts; School of Social Work; School of Computing & Engineering; School of Performing Arts; College of Health Professions; the Isabelle Farrington College of Education & Human Development; the Jack Welch College of Business & Technology; and the Dr. Susan L. Davis, RN, & Richard J. Henley College of Nursing. Sacred Heart, a Laudato Si\u2019 campus, stands out from other Catholic universities as it was established to be led by the laity. This contemporary Catholic university is rooted in the rich Catholic intellectual tradition and the liberal arts and, at the same time, cultivates students to be forward thinkers who enact change in their own lives, professions, and communities.\u202fSacred Heart University has earned national recognition for academic excellence, student success, career outcomes, and campus experience. The Princeton Review recognized SHU in its Best 392 Colleges: 2027 Edition and Best Business Schools: 2027 Edition, while additional national recognitions highlight the University\u2019s commitment to preparing students for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Sacred Heart is home to the award-winning, NPR-affiliate station, WSHU Public Radio; Division I athletics; and an impressive performing arts program that includes choir, band, dance, and theatre. www.sacredheart.edu View SHU\u2019s Faculty Experts Here Sacred Heart University\u2019s Department of Marketing in the AACSB-accredited Welch College of Business & Technology invites applications for Adjunct Instructors ready to bring the energy and evolution of marketing into the classroom and help students turn creativity, strategy, and emerging technology into real-world impact. Marketing never stands still. New technologies, platforms, and consumer expectations continually reshape how organizations connect with audiences and compete in the marketplace. This opportunity allows marketing professionals and scholars to share valuable expertise while challenging students to think creatively, build sound strategy, and connect foundational concepts with current tools and industry practices. Teaching opportunities span marketing, digital marketing, fashion marketing and merchandising, sales management, and event marketing and management. Programs include the Bachelor of Science in Marketing , Bachelor of Science in Fashion Marketing & Merchandising , and Master of Science in Digital Marketing , along with specialized minors, a graduate certificate, and an accelerated bachelor\u2019s-to-master\u2019s pathway. Additional information can be found in the Marketing course descriptions . Responsibilities: Teach assigned undergraduate or graduate marketing courses in accordance with established course objectives and academic standards Create an engaging and supportive learning environment Connect marketing theory with current industry practices, technologies, and emerging trends Provide students with timely feedback and maintain regular communication throughout the course Collaborate with the department chair and faculty as appropriate Fulfill all responsibilities associated with the assigned course Qualifications: A minimum of a master\u2019s degree in marketing, business, or a closely related field Academic or professional expertise relevant to the assigned course Prior college-level teaching experience is preferred Strong verbal, written, organizational, and interpersonal skills Commitment to fostering a collegial and supportive environment in which all members of the University community can thrive and succeed Application Instructions: Qualified applicants are invited to submit a letter of interest, current CV, statement of teaching philosophy, and relevant examples from courses taught (if applicable). Upon offer of employment, the selected candidate will be required to provide one formal letter of recommendation on professional letterhead and an official transcript reflecting their highest earned degree. Review of applications will be ongoing based on the needs of the department. Compensation & Benefits: The salary range for this position is\u00a0$4,300\u2013$5,400 per 3-credit course. Adjunct Instructors are not eligible to participate in the University\u2019s employee health and welfare benefit programs; however, they are eligible to participate in Sacred Heart University\u2019s 403(b) retirement plan, subject to the terms and eligibility requirements of the plan. Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Faculty Job Function Faculty Pay Type Salary Education Level Master\u2019s Degree Scan this QR code and apply! Download 3135 Easton Turnpike, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA \u00a92009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Cookie Preferences Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"}, "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/shu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/8411": {"title": "Information Technology", "description": "Information Technology - Systems Engineer | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs English (United States) Sign In Information Technology - Systems Engineer Req #945 3135 Easton Turnpike, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA Apply Share Job Description Posted Thursday, October 15, 2026 at 9:00 PM | Expires Monday, November 16, 2026 at 8:59 PM About Sacred Heart University As one of the nation\u2019s largest Catholic universities and among the fastest-growing private doctoral institutions in the U.S., Sacred Heart University is a national leader in shaping higher education for the 21st century. SHU offers more than 100 undergraduate, graduate and doctoral programs on its Fairfield, Conn., campus. Sacred Heart also has a campus in Dingle, Ireland, and offers online programs. Nearly 10,000 students attend the University\u2019s nine colleges and schools: College of Arts & Sciences; School of Communication, Media & the Arts; School of Social Work; School of Computing & Engineering; School of Performing Arts; College of Health Professions; the Isabelle Farrington College of Education & Human Development; the Jack Welch College of Business & Technology; and the Dr. Susan L. Davis, RN, & Richard J. Henley College of Nursing. Sacred Heart, a Laudato Si\u2019 campus, stands out from other Catholic universities as it was established to be led by the laity. This contemporary Catholic university is rooted in the rich Catholic intellectual tradition and the liberal arts and, at the same time, cultivates students to be forward thinkers who enact change in their own lives, professions, and communities.\u202fSacred Heart University has earned national recognition for academic excellence, student success, career outcomes, and campus experience. The Princeton Review recognized SHU in its Best 392 Colleges: 2027 Edition and Best Business Schools: 2027 Edition, while additional national recognitions highlight the University\u2019s commitment to preparing students for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Sacred Heart is home to the award-winning, NPR-affiliate station, WSHU Public Radio; Division I athletics; and an impressive performing arts program that includes choir, band, dance, and theatre . www.sacredheart.edu View SHU\u2019s Faculty Experts Here To apply: Qualified candidates are invited to submit a completed application and r\u00e9sum\u00e9 through the University's online application system. Applications submitted outside of the official Careers at SHU website will not be considered. Applicants should not apply through third-party or external job sites, as such postings may be fraudulent or may misrepresent opportunities that are no longer available at the University. A cover letter or statement of interest is preferred for all staff positions. Sacred Heart University complies with all federal and state employment laws and regulations. Applicants must be lawfully authorized to work for any employer in the United States. We are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa for this position Position Summary The Systems Engineer administers and supports enterprise application platforms and related systems. They also work with Infrastructure, IT Security, vendors, and internal teams to keep applications reliable, secure, and well documented. Principal Duties & Responsibilities Administer, maintain, and support enterprise application platforms and related tools including but not limited to Colleague, Papercut, PowerFaids, and more. Install, configure, upgrade, and patch assigned applications. Monitor application availability, performance, capacity, and overall health. Troubleshoot application, server, database, authentication, network, and integration issues. Maintain and patch servers supporting Enterprise Application Services applications, ensuring platform security, stability, and compatibility with assigned enterprise systems hosted in-house. Coordinate technical work with Infrastructure, IT Security, vendors, and internal teams. Support application implementations, upgrades, migrations, integrations, and recovery planning. Assist with security remediation, audits, backups, and business continuity activities. Automate routine administrative and monitoring tasks when practical. Maintain technical documentation, procedures, configurations, and support information. Communicate technical risks, dependencies, and recommendations Perform related duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities & Other Attributes Bachelor's degree in Information Technology, Computer Science, Information Systems, or a related field, or equivalent education and experience. Five to eight years of experience administering, upgrading, and supporting enterprise applications. Experience supporting applications in Windows and Linux environments. Working knowledge of Microsoft SQL Server, logs, queries, and monitoring tools used for troubleshooting. Knowledge of application security, identity and access management, certificates, service accounts, backups, and disaster recovery. Experience coordinating technical work across Infrastructure, IT Security, vendors, and business teams. Ability to automate routine tasks using PowerShell, Bash, Python, or similar tools is preferred. Experience with cloud-hosted, SaaS, or hybrid applications is preferred. Strong troubleshooting, communication, documentation, organization, and customer-service skills Ability to work independently, manage competing priorities, and respond to critical issues outside normal business hours when required. Unusual Working Conditions The Systems Engineer must be available to work some nights, weekends, or holidays when required. Pre-Employment Requirements All offers of employment are contingent upon satisfactory completion of a background check. Compensation & Benefits : The annual salary range for this position is $75,000 - $90,000. Sacred Heart University offers eligible employees a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, vision, life insurance, disability, retirement, paid time off, and other employee benefits. Specific benefits and eligibility requirements may vary based on the position and applicable plan provisions. This job posting provides an overview of the role's general nature and expected tasks. It is not meant to be a comprehensive list of all duties performed. The university reserves the right to modify or reassign job responsibilities at any time. This posting description does not constitute an employment contract, either explicit or implied. Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Staff Job Function Information Technology Pay Type Salary Education Level Bachelor\u2019s Degree Scan this QR code and apply! Download 3135 Easton Turnpike, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA \u00a92009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Cookie Preferences Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"}, "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/shu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/8404": {"title": "Public Safety", "description": "Public Safety - Lieutenant | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs English (United States) Sign In Public Safety - Lieutenant Req #936 5151 Park Ave, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA Apply Share Job Description Posted Thursday, October 15, 2026 at 9:00 PM | Expires Monday, November 16, 2026 at 8:59 PM About Sacred Heart University As one of the nation\u2019s largest Catholic universities and among the fastest-growing private doctoral institutions in the U.S., Sacred Heart University is a national leader in shaping higher education for the 21st century. SHU offers more than 100 undergraduate, graduate and doctoral programs on its Fairfield, Conn., campus. Sacred Heart also has a campus in Dingle, Ireland, and offers online programs. Nearly 10,000 students attend the University\u2019s nine colleges and schools: College of Arts & Sciences; School of Communication, Media & the Arts; School of Social Work; School of Computing & Engineering; School of Performing Arts; College of Health Professions; the Isabelle Farrington College of Education & Human Development; the Jack Welch College of Business & Technology; and the Dr. Susan L. Davis, RN, & Richard J. Henley College of Nursing. Sacred Heart, a Laudato Si\u2019 campus, stands out from other Catholic universities as it was established to be led by the laity. This contemporary Catholic university is rooted in the rich Catholic intellectual tradition and the liberal arts and, at the same time, cultivates students to be forward thinkers who enact change in their own lives, professions, and communities.\u202fSacred Heart University has earned national recognition for academic excellence, student success, career outcomes, and campus experience. The Princeton Review recognized SHU in its Best 392 Colleges: 2027 Edition and Best Business Schools: 2027 Edition, while additional national recognitions highlight the University\u2019s commitment to preparing students for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Sacred Heart is home to the award-winning, NPR-affiliate station, WSHU Public Radio; Division I athletics; and an impressive performing arts program that includes choir, band, dance, and theatre . www.sacredheart.edu View SHU\u2019s Faculty Experts Here To apply: Qualified candidates are invited to submit a completed application and r\u00e9sum\u00e9 through the University's online application system. Applications submitted outside of the official Careers at SHU website will not be considered. Applicants should not apply through third-party or external job sites, as such postings may be fraudulent or may misrepresent opportunities that are no longer available at the University. A cover letter or statement of interest is preferred for all staff positions. Sacred Heart University complies with all federal and state employment laws and regulations. Applicants must be lawfully authorized to work for any employer in the United States. We are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa for this position Position Summary To provide for the safety and security of all members of the University community. To provide for the physical security of University property & enforce University and Departmental rules and regulations.\u00a0 Oversee the daily functions of DPS officers and contract security officers to ensure all services are delivered in a consistent, professional, and timely manner. Principal Duties & Responsibilities Position will have operational and administrative oversight of assigned shift(s). Must embrace a community policing/problem-solving approach to patrol responsibilities. Must be capable of Patrolling University properties via foot, bicycle, or vehicle. Plan, supervise, and review the activities of all shift personnel, including shift officers, regarding duties, posts, patrol areas, and dispatch to achieve maximum resource efficiency. Conduct daily shift-level briefing sessions and line inspections to ensure all personnel are properly informed and properly equipped to perform their daily duties. Supervise and direct front-line Public Safety officer response to calls for service and emergency incidents, including, but not limited to, fire alarms/fires, medical incidents, weather emergencies, motor vehicle accidents, disturbances, altercations, etc. May issue Timely Warnings or Crime Notices to the community in compliance with Clery Act mandates. Adheres to the University and the Department of Public Safety\u2019s rules, regulations, responsibilities, and procedures and ensures all assigned personnel do so as well. Complies with and is respectful of Superiors and their instructions, directives, and assignments. Keep superiors informed of performance or personnel issues and initiate and/or carry out appropriate corrective action, counseling, and training. Submits thorough and timely reports documenting any personnel matters, unusual occurrences, complaints, and/or crimes/incidents. Maintains a professional, formal, and approachable demeanor while on duty to foster effective public relations while interacting within the University community. Provide aid or services to the University community, including personal safety escorts, motor vehicle assistance, and room/bldg. locking/unlocking, bank runs, etc. \u2026 Interact professionally with all internal University members and external municipal partners/agencies (police, fire, ambulance, etc.). May be required to work special assignments, events, shifts, and extended hours depending upon the needs of the agency. May be required to fulfill Dispatch duties if needed. Assist in the development and delivery of safety and emergency management training programs for department personnel and the university community. Will not act, either on duty or off duty, in any manner that is detrimental, in the view of SHU, to the Mission or reputation of Sacred Heart University. Must maintain all applicable certifications and licensing, including firearm requirements, training, and ongoing qualifications. Essential physical job tasks include sitting, standing, or walking for sustained periods of time; climbing up/downstairs; bending, turning, reaching, and grasping. Visual acuity sufficient for reading ID cards/written materials, Hearing sufficient for perceiving sounds at normal speaking levels. Be able to work in various positions, including but not limited to stooping, standing, bending over, sitting, kneeling, and squatting for extended periods of time. Be able to lift (indicate the weight minimum), pull, and push materials and equipment to complete the assigned job task. May be required to work in extreme outdoor weather conditions (heat, snow, ice, rain, etc.). Perform other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities, & Other Attributes Associate degree in Criminal Justice or related field. Appropriate Law Enforcement experience may be substituted for a degree. Minimum of ten years of law enforcement or military experience required, or comparable public security experience. Minimum of two years serving in a supervisory level law enforcement position or comparable leadership position in a non-law enforcement agency. Must have separated from law enforcement/military service in good standing. Must hold a valid State Driver\u2019s License and maintain a satisfactory driving record. Possess and maintain: CT State Security Guard Card and Class 1 License endorsement, or other comparable certification as may be required. If former LEO must be capable of meeting standards established by the Law Enforcement Officer\u2019s Safety Act (HR-218). Proficiency in Microsoft Office products (including Word, Excel, Outlook, and PowerPoint). Excellent written and verbal communication skills. EMR/EMT certification Essential physical job tasks include walking, climbing stairs, driving emergency vehicles, conducting foot patrols in buildings, parking lots, and campus fields, and standing or moving for extended periods.\u00a0 Breaking up fights or preventing physical altercations. Directing large crowds during events or emergencies. Positioning barricades or moving equipment to manage public spaces and checkpoints.\u00a0 Directing traffic flow and setting up detours or roadblocks. Carrying and using protective gear and fire extinguishers. Administering CPR or first aid or using automated external defibrillators (AEDs). Carrying medical supplies to assist during emergencies and transporting patients or individuals needing help. Unusual Working Conditions May require working different shifts at various university campuses or facilities. May require working on weekends, holidays, and in adverse weather conditions. Pre-Employment Requirements All offers of employment are contingent upon satisfactory completion of a background check. In accordance with Connecticut General Statutes \u00a7 31-51v, applicants selected for this position will be required to undergo a pre-employment drug test as a condition of employment. Employment is contingent upon satisfactory results of both the background check and drug test. Compensation & Benefits : The annual salary range for this position is $51,750 - $66,000. Sacred Heart University offers eligible employees a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, vision, life insurance, disability, retirement, paid time off, and other employee benefits. Specific benefits and eligibility requirements may vary based on the position and applicable plan provisions. This job posting provides an overview of the role's general nature and expected tasks. It is not meant to be a comprehensive list of all duties performed. The university reserves the right to modify or reassign job responsibilities at any time. This posting description does not constitute an employment contract, either explicit or implied. Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Staff Pay Type Salary Education Level Associate Degree Scan this QR code and apply! Download 5151 Park Ave, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA \u00a92009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Cookie Preferences Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"}, "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/shu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/8393": {"title": "Management - Tenure-Track Assistant Professor", "description": "Management - Tenure-Track Assistant Professor | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs English (United States) Sign In Management - Tenure-Track Assistant Professor Req #942 3135 Easton Turnpike, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA Apply Share Job Description Posted Thursday, October 15, 2026 at 9:00 PM About Sacred Heart University As one of the nation\u2019s largest Catholic universities and among the fastest-growing private doctoral institutions in the U.S., Sacred Heart University is a national leader in shaping higher education for the 21st century. SHU offers more than 100 undergraduate, graduate and doctoral programs on its Fairfield, Conn., campus. Sacred Heart also has a campus in Dingle, Ireland, and offers online programs. Nearly 10,000 students attend the University\u2019s nine colleges and schools: College of Arts & Sciences; School of Communication, Media & the Arts; School of Social Work; School of Computing & Engineering; School of Performing Arts; College of Health Professions; the Isabelle Farrington College of Education & Human Development; the Jack Welch College of Business & Technology; and the Dr. Susan L. Davis, RN, & Richard J. Henley College of Nursing. Sacred Heart, a Laudato Si\u2019 campus, stands out from other Catholic universities as it was established to be led by the laity. This contemporary Catholic university is rooted in the rich Catholic intellectual tradition and the liberal arts and, at the same time, cultivates students to be forward thinkers who enact change in their own lives, professions, and communities.\u202fSacred Heart University has earned national recognition for academic excellence, student success, career outcomes, and campus experience. The Princeton Review recognized SHU in its Best 392 Colleges: 2027 Edition and Best Business Schools: 2027 Edition, while additional national recognitions highlight the University\u2019s commitment to preparing students for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Sacred Heart is home to the award-winning, NPR-affiliate station, WSHU Public Radio; Division I athletics; and an impressive performing arts program that includes choir, band, dance, and theatre. www.sacredheart.edu View SHU\u2019s Faculty Experts Here Sacred Heart University\u2019s Department of Management in the Welch College of Business & Technology invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor of Management, beginning Fall 2027 , pending final budgetary approval. We seek an engaged scholar and educator specializing in Entrepreneurship, Strategy, or Innovation who is passionate about creating an exceptional student experience and contributing to the department's innovative and entrepreneurial culture. We are particularly interested in candidates whose research, teaching, or professional interests include artificial intelligence, technology management, and emerging technologies, and who can contribute to the development of new courses, programs, and student experiences in these areas. The Department of Management brings together faculty with expertise in strategy, organizational behavior, entrepreneurship, innovation, human resource management, operations and supply chain management, business law, and international management. The department offers a B.S. in Management, supports several undergraduate minors, and contributes to the College's MBA program. Across these programs, faculty emphasize rigorous scholarship, student-centered teaching, and active, experiential learning. Faculty also have opportunities to connect teaching, scholarship, and community engagement through initiatives such as the Pioneer Pitch Competition , the peer-reviewed New England Journal of Entrepreneurship , and collaborations with SHU's Center for Nonprofits . Teaching & Student Engagement: Excellence in teaching is central to the department\u2019s mission. We seek candidates who create engaging, rigorous learning environments that strengthen students\u2019 critical thinking, leadership, ethical reasoning, and managerial decision-making. Teaching opportunities include undergraduate and graduate management courses aligned with departmental needs and the candidate\u2019s expertise. Candidates interested in developing courses related to artificial intelligence, emerging technologies, innovation, and technology management are particularly encouraged to apply. Additional information can be found in the Management course descriptions . The department emphasizes active and experiential learning, connecting management concepts with real organizational and entrepreneurial\u00a0challenges through case studies, projects, simulations, competitions, and business and community partnerships. We especially value faculty who enjoy mentoring students, encouraging entrepreneurial thinking, and connecting classroom learning with professional practice. An interest in incorporating data, analytics, and emerging technologies into management education is a plus. Scholarship: The successful candidate will be expected to develop and maintain an active scholarly agenda and contribute to the intellectual life of the department and College. We value meaningful scholarship that informs management practice, advances academic research, and connects with teaching and student learning. We particularly welcome research interests in entrepreneurship, strategy, innovation, technology management, artificial intelligence, and the organizational implications of emerging technologies. Collaborative and interdisciplinary research across business and technology disciplines is encouraged. Responsibilities: Advise and mentor undergraduate and/or graduate students; Contribute to curriculum development, course revision, assessment, and continuous program improvement; Participate actively in departmental, college, and university service; Support experiential learning; Contribute to the intellectual and collegial life of the department; and Support the continued development and visibility of the department\u2019s programs. Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. in Management, with a specialization in Entrepreneurship, Strategic Management, Innovation, or a closely related management discipline, from an AACSB-accredited institution, completed by the start of the appointment. Evidence of, or strong potential for, excellence in university-level teaching aligned with the candidate's expertise. Demonstrated commitment to student engagement, mentoring, and experiential learning. Evidence of, or potential for, maintaining an active program of scholarly research. Candidates who are ABD will be considered, provided there is strong evidence that all doctoral requirements will be completed before the start of the appointment. Application Instructions: Qualified applicants are invited to submit the following materials through Sacred Heart University's online application portal: A letter of application outlining relevant qualifications, experience, and interest in the position. Curriculum vitae. Statement of teaching philosophy. Statement of research interests. Evidence of teaching effectiveness, if available. Contact information for three professional references. Three formal letters of recommendation on professional letterhead and an official transcript reflecting the highest conferred degree will be required upon offer of employment. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Initial interviews will be conducted virtually, followed by on-campus interviews for selected candidates. Questions regarding the position may be directed to the Search Committee Chair, Dr. Michael Zhang, at ZhangM@sacredheart.edu . Compensation & Benefits: The salary range for this position is $96,324-$135,986. Sacred Heart University offers eligible employees a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, vision, life insurance, disability, retirement, paid time off, and other employee benefits. Specific benefits and eligibility requirements may vary based on the position and applicable plan provisions. Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Faculty Job Function Faculty Pay Type Salary Education Level Doctorate Hiring Min Rate 96,324 USD Hiring Max Rate 135,986 USD Scan this QR code and apply! Download 3135 Easton Turnpike, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA \u00a92009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Cookie Preferences Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"}, "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/shu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/8364": {"title": "Speech, Language & Hearing Sciences - Assistant Professor", "description": "Speech, Language & Hearing Sciences - Assistant Professor | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs English (United States) Sign In Speech, Language & Hearing Sciences - Assistant Professor Req #943 4000 Park Ave, Bridgeport, CT 06604, USA Apply Share Job Description Posted Monday, October 12, 2026 at 9:00 PM About Sacred Heart University As one of the nation\u2019s largest Catholic universities and among the fastest-growing private doctoral institutions in the U.S., Sacred Heart University is a national leader in shaping higher education for the 21st century. SHU offers more than 100 undergraduate, graduate and doctoral programs on its Fairfield, Conn., campus. Sacred Heart also has a campus in Dingle, Ireland, and offers online programs. Nearly 10,000 students attend the University\u2019s nine colleges and schools: College of Arts & Sciences; School of Communication, Media & the Arts; School of Social Work; School of Computing & Engineering; School of Performing Arts; College of Health Professions; the Isabelle Farrington College of Education & Human Development; the Jack Welch College of Business & Technology; and the Dr. Susan L. Davis, RN, & Richard J. Henley College of Nursing. Sacred Heart, a Laudato Si\u2019 campus, stands out from other Catholic universities as it was established to be led by the laity. This contemporary Catholic university is rooted in the rich Catholic intellectual tradition and the liberal arts and, at the same time, cultivates students to be forward thinkers who enact change in their own lives, professions, and communities.\u202fSacred Heart University has earned national recognition for academic excellence, student success, career outcomes, and campus experience. The Princeton Review recognized SHU in its Best 392 Colleges: 2027 Edition and Best Business Schools: 2027 Edition, while additional national recognitions highlight the University\u2019s commitment to preparing students for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Sacred Heart is home to the award-winning, NPR-affiliate station, WSHU Public Radio; Division I athletics; and an impressive performing arts program that includes choir, band, dance, and theatre. www.sacredheart.edu View SHU\u2019s Faculty Experts Here Sacred Heart University\u2019s Department of Speech, Language & Hearing Sciences in the College of Health Professions invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor. We seek an educator-scholar committed to excellence in teaching, student mentorship, scholarly research, and service who will contribute to student success, the advancement of the discipline, and the continued development of our academic programs. This 10-month faculty appointment offers the opportunity to engage with undergraduate and graduate students, contribute to curriculum development and program assessment, and pursue scholarly interests within a collaborative academic environment. The successful candidate will support student learning and professional development while contributing to the College\u2019s mission and the broader University community. Responsibilities: Teach assigned undergraduate and/or graduate courses using effective, evidence-based, and inclusive teaching approaches appropriate to the discipline and course format. Contribute to course and curriculum development, program assessment, and continuous improvement. Advise and mentor students in academic planning, professional development, and career preparation, including supervision of scholarly, capstone, practicum, internship, or other experiential learning activities, as appropriate. Establish and maintain an active program of scholarship and/or creative activity, including dissemination of scholarly work and pursuit of internal or external funding, as appropriate. Participate in departmental, College, University, and professional service, including faculty governance, committees, accreditation activities, and related initiatives. Support student recruitment, retention, engagement, and academic success. Maintain current disciplinary and pedagogical expertise through ongoing professional development. Foster an inclusive, collaborative, and collegial academic environment that supports student learning and upholds professional and academic standards. Minimum Qualifications: Earned Ph.D. or imminent ABD with expected completion by August 2027 in Speech, Language, and Hearing Sciences or related field. Application Instructions: Qualified applicants are invited to submit the following materials through Sacred Heart University's online application portal: A letter of application outlining relevant qualifications, experience, and interest in the position. Curriculum vitae. Statement of teaching philosophy. Statement of research interests. Three formal letters of recommendation on professional letterhead and an official transcript reflecting the highest conferred degree will be required upon offer of employment. Compensation & Benefits: The salary range for this position is $95,659-$135,048. Sacred Heart University offers eligible employees a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, vision, life insurance, disability, retirement, paid time off, and other employee benefits. Specific benefits and eligibility requirements may vary based on the position and applicable plan provisions. Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Faculty Job Function Faculty Pay Type Salary Education Level Doctorate Hiring Min Rate 95,659 USD Hiring Max Rate 135,048 USD Scan this QR code and apply! Download 4000 Park Ave, Bridgeport, CT 06604, USA \u00a92009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Cookie Preferences Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"}, "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/shu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/8356": {"title": "Speech, Language & Hearing Sciences - Assistant or Associate Professor", "description": "Speech, Language & Hearing Sciences - Assistant or Associate Professor | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs English (United States) Sign In Speech, Language & Hearing Sciences - Assistant or Associate Professor Req #944 4000 Park Ave, Bridgeport, CT 06604, USA Apply Share Job Description Posted Monday, October 12, 2026 at 9:00 PM About Sacred Heart University As one of the nation\u2019s largest Catholic universities and among the fastest-growing private doctoral institutions in the U.S., Sacred Heart University is a national leader in shaping higher education for the 21st century. SHU offers more than 100 undergraduate, graduate and doctoral programs on its Fairfield, Conn., campus. Sacred Heart also has a campus in Dingle, Ireland, and offers online programs. Nearly 10,000 students attend the University\u2019s nine colleges and schools: College of Arts & Sciences; School of Communication, Media & the Arts; School of Social Work; School of Computing & Engineering; School of Performing Arts; College of Health Professions; the Isabelle Farrington College of Education & Human Development; the Jack Welch College of Business & Technology; and the Dr. Susan L. Davis, RN, & Richard J. Henley College of Nursing. Sacred Heart, a Laudato Si\u2019 campus, stands out from other Catholic universities as it was established to be led by the laity. This contemporary Catholic university is rooted in the rich Catholic intellectual tradition and the liberal arts and, at the same time, cultivates students to be forward thinkers who enact change in their own lives, professions, and communities.\u202fSacred Heart University has earned national recognition for academic excellence, student success, career outcomes, and campus experience. The Princeton Review recognized SHU in its Best 392 Colleges: 2027 Edition and Best Business Schools: 2027 Edition, while additional national recognitions highlight the University\u2019s commitment to preparing students for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Sacred Heart is home to the award-winning, NPR-affiliate station, WSHU Public Radio; Division I athletics; and an impressive performing arts program that includes choir, band, dance, and theatre. www.sacredheart.edu View SHU\u2019s Faculty Experts Here Sacred Heart University\u2019s Department of Speech, Language & Hearing Sciences in the College of Health Professions invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant or Associate Professor. We seek an educator-scholar committed to excellence in teaching, student mentorship, scholarly research, and service who will contribute to the continued development of our academic programs and the advancement of speech-language pathology and hearing sciences. This 10-month faculty appointment offers the opportunity to engage with undergraduate and graduate students, contribute to curriculum development and program assessment, and pursue scholarly interests within a collaborative academic environment. The successful candidate will support student learning and professional development while contributing to the College\u2019s mission and the broader University community. This is an open-rank position, with the appointment level determined by the candidate\u2019s qualifications and the applicable criteria outlined in the Faculty Handbook. Responsibilities: Provide high-quality instruction in assigned undergraduate and/or graduate courses using effective, evidence-based, and inclusive teaching approaches appropriate to the discipline and course format. Contribute to course and curriculum development, program improvement, and assessment of student learning. Advise and mentor students in their academic progress, professional development, and career preparation, including supervision of scholarly, capstone, practicum, internship, or other experiential learning activities, as appropriate. Maintain an active program of scholarship and/or creative activity, including dissemination of scholarly work and pursuit of internal or external funding, as appropriate. Participate in departmental, College, University, and professional service, including faculty governance, committees, accreditation activities, and related initiatives. Support student recruitment, retention, engagement, and academic success. Maintain and advance disciplinary and pedagogical expertise through ongoing professional development and engagement with the profession. Foster an inclusive, collaborative, and collegial academic environment that supports student learning and upholds professional and academic standards. Minimum Qualifications: Earned Ph.D. in Speech, Language, and Hearing Sciences or a related field. College or university level teaching experience, particularly in speech-language pathology. Established or emerging scholarly expertise in an area related to speech-language pathology and/or hearing sciences. Application Instructions: Qualified applicants are invited to submit the following materials through Sacred Heart University's online application portal: A letter of application outlining relevant qualifications, experience, and interest in the position. Curriculum vitae. Statement of teaching philosophy. Statement of research interests. Three formal letters of recommendation on professional letterhead and an official transcript reflecting the highest conferred degree will be required upon offer of employment. Compensation & Benefits: The salary range for this position is $95,659-$135,048. Sacred Heart University offers eligible employees a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, vision, life insurance, disability, retirement, paid time off, and other employee benefits. Specific benefits and eligibility requirements may vary based on the position and applicable plan provisions. Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Faculty Job Function Faculty Pay Type Salary Education Level Doctorate Hiring Min Rate 95,659 USD Hiring Max Rate 135,048 USD Scan this QR code and apply! Download 4000 Park Ave, Bridgeport, CT 06604, USA \u00a92009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Cookie Preferences Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"}, "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/shu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/8346": {"title": "Horizons - Administrative Assistant", "description": "Horizons - Administrative Assistant | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs English (United States) Sign In Horizons - Administrative Assistant Req #940 3135 Easton Turnpike, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA Apply Share Job Description Posted Monday, October 12, 2026 at 9:00 PM | Expires Tuesday, October 20, 2026 at 8:59 PM About Sacred Heart University As one of the nation\u2019s largest Catholic universities and among the fastest-growing private doctoral institutions in the U.S., Sacred Heart University is a national leader in shaping higher education for the 21st century. SHU offers more than 100 undergraduate, graduate and doctoral programs on its Fairfield, Conn., campus. Sacred Heart also has a campus in Dingle, Ireland, and offers online programs. Nearly 10,000 students attend the University\u2019s nine colleges and schools: College of Arts & Sciences; School of Communication, Media & the Arts; School of Social Work; School of Computing & Engineering; School of Performing Arts; College of Health Professions; the Isabelle Farrington College of Education & Human Development; the Jack Welch College of Business & Technology; and the Dr. Susan L. Davis, RN, & Richard J. Henley College of Nursing. Sacred Heart, a Laudato Si\u2019 campus, stands out from other Catholic universities as it was established to be led by the laity. This contemporary Catholic university is rooted in the rich Catholic intellectual tradition and the liberal arts and, at the same time, cultivates students to be forward thinkers who enact change in their own lives, professions, and communities.\u202fSacred Heart University has earned national recognition for academic excellence, student success, career outcomes, and campus experience. The Princeton Review recognized SHU in its Best 392 Colleges: 2027 Edition and Best Business Schools: 2027 Edition, while additional national recognitions highlight the University\u2019s commitment to preparing students for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Sacred Heart is home to the award-winning, NPR-affiliate station, WSHU Public Radio; Division I athletics; and an impressive performing arts program that includes choir, band, dance, and theatre . www.sacredheart.edu View SHU\u2019s Faculty Experts Here To apply: Qualified candidates are invited to submit a completed application and r\u00e9sum\u00e9 through the University's online application system. Applications submitted outside of the official Careers at SHU website will not be considered. Applicants should not apply through third-party or external job sites, as such postings may be fraudulent or may misrepresent opportunities that are no longer available at the University. A cover letter or statement of interest is preferred for all staff positions. Sacred Heart University complies with all federal and state employment laws and regulations. Applicants must be lawfully authorized to work for any employer in the United States. We are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa for this position Position Summary The Administrative Assistant provides daily administrative support for Horizons Sacred Heart University, a year-round program serving Bridgeport students and families across its PreK\u201312 continuum. The position serves as a primary point of contact for families and campus partners and coordinates family communications, admissions and re-enrollment processes, purchasing, program schedules and records, and meeting and event logistics. The Administrative Assistant maintains accurate information, tracks deadlines, and refers decisions and approvals to the Executive Director or appropriate Program Manager. Principal Duties & Responsibilities Family communications: Monitor shared inboxes, phone calls, and inquiries; answer routine questions using approved information; draft, proofread, and distribute family notices through ParentSquare and other approved channels; maintain contact lists and communication logs; refer sensitive matters and policy exceptions to the appropriate leader. Admissions and re-enrollment: Schedule admissions appointments, family meetings, and orientations; distribute and track applications, consent forms, and enrollment and re-enrollment materials; follow up on missing items; maintain applicant records and waitlists; and prepare enrollment status reports. Program leaders make admissions, placement, and exception decisions. Purchasing and supplies: Collect approved supply requests, obtain quotes when needed, enter orders through SHU systems, track deliveries and inventory, and submit invoices and supporting records for review. Purchasing and vendor commitments remain subject to the Executive Director\u2019s approval and SHU procedures. Program scheduling and records: Maintain student schedules and program rosters; communicate approved assignments to families and staff; prepare program materials and spaces; record attendance; and coordinate assessment schedules and materials. Maintain program calendars, student records, and routine reports. Carry out this work under the direction of the Program Managers, who make decisions about student services and programming. Meetings and events: Schedule meetings and maintain event timelines, invitations, RSVP lists, materials, and follow-up tasks. Coordinate logistics for the annual benefit, family activities, Board meetings, and outreach in partnership with University Advancement and SHU Events. The Executive Director retains responsibility for messaging, fundraising, sponsor commitments, and event budgets. Campus and office coordination: Reserve rooms and submit facilities, IT, catering, and other campus service requests; coordinate with SHU departments and vendors on approved logistics; maintain organized shared files; and track administrative forms and renewal deadlines. Other duties: Support special projects and perform related administrative tasks as assigned by the Executive Director. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities & Other Attributes High school diploma or equivalent required Experience in an educational or nonprofit setting helpful. Strong written and verbal communication, organization, accuracy, follow-through, discretion, and ability to manage multiple deadlines. Proficiency with Microsoft Office and Outlook; ability to learn ParentSquare, Salesforce, SHU purchasing systems, and student or donor record systems. Ability to work respectfully with families, students, colleagues, and campus partners; occasional evening or weekend support for scheduled program events may be required. Pre-Employment Requirements All offers of employment are contingent upon satisfactory completion of a background check. Compensation & Benefits : The annual salary range for this position is $42,770-$52,729 Sacred Heart University offers eligible employees a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, vision, life insurance, disability, retirement, paid time off, and other employee benefits. Specific benefits and eligibility requirements may vary based on the position and applicable plan provisions. This job posting provides an overview of the role's general nature and expected tasks. It is not meant to be a comprehensive list of all duties performed. The university reserves the right to modify or reassign job responsibilities at any time. This posting description does not constitute an employment contract, either explicit or implied. Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Staff Job Function Administrative Support Pay Type Salary Education Level High School Scan this QR code and apply! Download 3135 Easton Turnpike, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA \u00a92009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Cookie Preferences Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"}}, "rows": {"https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com